  "about": "The contract of the French phonetic key. 'collide' groups must all get the same key; 'differ' pairs must get different keys; 'known_shared' pairs are masculine and feminine first names that are the same sound in French and that no rule can separate (the sex rule of lot 2 bis lists them instead of hiding them); 'observe' names are only printed in the collision table. Add a row, run: cargo test --test knowledge_names -- --nocapture. A collision is a hint to the resolver (a 'did you mean'), never a merge. Names are invented or very common, or come from the Insee lists of surnames and first names (aggregates); none is a real person's record. 'false_friends' are pairs the owner judged to be two different names that the key still cannot separate (kept so that the limit is measured, and so that a rule that separates them is noticed).",
